{
 "why": "THE MEASUREMENT: `trustedTypes.getTypeMapping()`, read whole off Chrome 150.0.7871.46, Brave 151.1.93.138, Edge 151.0.4129.93 and Opera 135.0.5973.133 on 2026-09-19/20 (PARITY FP5.5), headed under Xvfb over CDP with --remote-debugging-port=<a free port> (never =0, which sets navigator.webdriver; it read false in every run), at TWO origins -- http://127.0.0.1:<p>/ and http://web-platform.test:<p>/ -- which agreed byte for byte, so this is not origin-dependent. It is the one table `getTypeMapping`, `getAttributeType` and `getPropertyType` all three read, because a second copy of a measurement is a second definition. WHY IT IS NOT DERIVED FROM THE ENGINE'S OWN ROWS: the `any_element.attributes` list is Blink's whole event-handler-name set, not this window's -- the union of every `on*` member the active capture records is 125 names and the union over korvus's whole registry is 279, against the 321 the browsers list, and `getAttributeType('div','onbogus')` answers null, so it is a LIST and not the rule `starts with on`. WHY IT IS NOT A BUNDLE FIELD: it is a platform fact of the Chromium build, not of the device, and the capture rig does not record it at all. WHAT PUTS AN ENTRY IN: re-run the reading above on a newer build. WHAT TAKES ONE OUT: the same reading no longer listing it. Each attribute name maps to the browsers that list it; the engine publishes the names ALL FOUR list, and `browsers` is what names the rest.",
 "measured": "2026-09-20",
 "versions": {
  "brave-151": "Brave Browser 151.1.93.138 unknown",
  "chrome-150": "Google Chrome 150.0.7871.46",
  "edge-151": "Microsoft Edge 151.0.4129.93",
  "opera-135": "135.0.5973.133"
 },
 "origins": {
  "secure": "http://127.0.0.1:<port>/page.html",
  "insecure": "http://web-platform.test:<port>/page.html"
 },
 "namespaces": {
  "why": "getAttributeType(tag, attr, elementNs, attrNs) and getPropertyType(tag, prop, elementNs) resolve against the element's NAMESPACE. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-22 (TT1) against Brave 151.1.93.138 and Chrome 150.0.7871.46 headless --dump-dom, which answered IDENTICALLY on all 32 probes, and read against Blink's own FindEntryInAttributeTypeVector (third_party/blink/renderer/core/trustedtypes/trusted_type_policy_factory.cc:180). The 2026-09-20 reading below it generalised THREE rules from cases it had not probed and all three were wrong; what the browsers actually do is: (1) elementNs absent OR '' is the XHTML namespace, so the `html` element rows apply; the SVG namespace reads `svg`; no other namespace has element rows. (2) attrNs absent OR '' is the NULL namespace and matches every row that carries no attribute namespace -- it does NOT answer null, which is what the earlier reading said; only a non-empty attrNs that is not a row's own answers null. (3) ONE row carries an attribute namespace: SVG `script`'s `href` in the XLink namespace (Blink's xlink_names::kHrefAttr entry), so getAttributeType('script','href',svgNs,xlinkNs) is TrustedScriptURL. (4) The `*` ATTRIBUTE row applies in the XHTML, SVG **and MathML** namespaces and nowhere else (Blink `matches_star_atom`), which is why MathML -- a namespace with no element rows at all -- still answers TrustedScript for an event handler. (5) The `*` PROPERTY rows apply in EVERY namespace without exception, including XUL and a made-up one: getPropertyType('foo','innerHTML', xulNs) is TrustedHTML (Blink exempts the property vector from `matches_star_atom` outright). Both namespace strings are compared CASE-SENSITIVELY. The tag and the ATTRIBUTE name are ASCII-lowercased before the lookup ('SCRIPT'/'SRC'/'onClick' all match); the PROPERTY name is not ('INNERHTML' and 'codebase' answer null where 'innerHTML' and 'codeBase' answer a type). The attribute name is a LOCAL name: 'xlink:href' answers null where 'href' answers a type. getTypeMapping() itself answers this whole map for no argument and for '', and null for any namespace string including the XHTML one.",
  "html": "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml",
  "mathml": "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML",
  "svg": "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg",
  "xlink": "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
 },
 "get_type_mapping": {
  "why": "What `getTypeMapping()` itself returns, verbatim -- a FRESH plain object each call (measured: `getTypeMapping() !== getTypeMapping()`), whose prototype is Object.prototype. The `script` entry merges the two namespaces' attributes, which is the browser's own shape: `href` is there although getAttributeType('script','href') answers null in HTML and TrustedScriptURL in SVG.",
  "elements": {
   "embed": {
    "attributes": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "properties": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   },
   "iframe": {
    "attributes": {
     "srcdoc": "TrustedHTML"
    },
    "properties": {
     "srcdoc": "TrustedHTML"
    }
   },
   "object": {
    "attributes": {
     "codebase": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "data": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "properties": {
     "codeBase": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "data": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   },
   "script": {
    "attributes": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "href": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "properties": {
     "innerText": "TrustedScript",
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "text": "TrustedScript",
     "textContent": "TrustedScript",
     "href": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   }
  },
  "any_element_properties": {
   "innerHTML": "TrustedHTML",
   "outerHTML": "TrustedHTML"
  }
 },
 "resolve": {
  "why": "What getAttributeType / getPropertyType answer, per NAMESPACE -- measured one (tag, name, namespace) at a time, because the merged map above cannot express it.",
  "html": {
   "attributes": {
    "embed": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "iframe": {
     "srcdoc": "TrustedHTML"
    },
    "object": {
     "codebase": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "data": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "script": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   },
   "properties": {
    "embed": {
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "iframe": {
     "srcdoc": "TrustedHTML"
    },
    "object": {
     "codeBase": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "data": "TrustedScriptURL"
    },
    "script": {
     "innerText": "TrustedScript",
     "src": "TrustedScriptURL",
     "text": "TrustedScript",
     "textContent": "TrustedScript"
    }
   }
  },
  "svg": {
   "attributes": {
    "script": {
     "href": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   },
   "attributes_ns": {
    "why": "Rows whose ATTRIBUTE carries a namespace, keyed by that namespace URI -- everything in `attributes` above is in the null one. Blink's table has exactly one such row in either namespace, `{svg_names::kScriptTag, xlink_names::kHrefAttr}` (trusted_type_policy_factory.cc:68), and Brave 151 / Chrome 150 both answer TrustedScriptURL for getAttributeType('script','href',svgNs,xlinkNs) and null for any other attrNs. Keyed by URI rather than by a name like `xlink` so the URI stays in the measurement and not in the code.",
    "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink": {
     "script": {
      "href": "TrustedScriptURL"
     }
    }
   },
   "properties": {
    "script": {
     "href": "TrustedScriptURL"
    }
   }
  },
  "any_element": {
   "why": "The `*` rows -- and the ATTRIBUTE one and the PROPERTY ones do NOT have the same reach, which is the defect TT1 closed. The `*` ATTRIBUTE row applies only when the ELEMENT namespace is one of `attribute_element_namespaces` below: XHTML, SVG and MathML. MathML is the whole reason that list exists -- it has no element rows of its own, so a lookup that stops when no element table matches never reaches this row and getAttributeType('mrow','onmousedown',mathmlNs) answers null instead of TrustedScript. The `*` PROPERTY rows have NO such list: they apply in every namespace whatever, measured getPropertyType('foo','innerHTML', xulNs) == 'TrustedHTML' (Blink exempts the property vector from `matches_star_atom` outright, trusted_type_policy_factory.cc:194). The `*` attribute row carries no attribute namespace, so only a null or empty attrNs reaches it. The event-handler attribute names are `event_handler_attributes` below; they are NOT properties (getPropertyType('div','onclick') answers null).",
   "attribute_element_namespaces": [
    "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml",
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg",
    "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"
   ],
   "properties": {
    "innerHTML": "TrustedHTML",
    "outerHTML": "TrustedHTML"
   },
   "attribute_type": "TrustedScript"
  }
 },
